<title>USA: Amex says Mexico to hear its Visa complaint.</title>
<headline>Amex says Mexico to hear its Visa complaint.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Express Co said on Tuesday that the Federal Competition Commission of Mexico has decided to open proceedings on its complaint accusing credit-card rival  Visa International of engaging in anti-competitive practices in the country.</p>
<p>American Express also said the commission has issued a preliminary injunction against Visa allegedly taking action to prohibit member banks from issuing American Express card products.</p>
<p>American Express has taken similar action in the past two weeks in Argentina, Brazil, Colombia, Chile and Puerto Rico.  </p>
<p>Visa could not be reached immediately for comment. However, it has denied American Express allegations in the past.</p>
</text>
